From 6ca3be32f48e8ad6061b17949baef8f763957f3d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Iori Yanokura <ab.ioryz@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 21 Sep 2026 14:51:37 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 5/6] hw/arm: Add Renesas RA4M1 SoC and Arduino UNO R4 board

Add the RA4M1 (R7FA4M1AB, Cortex-M4F) with its ICU, SCI0/1/2/9, AGT0/1
and I/O ports, plus the arduino-uno-r4 board that boots sketches built by
the Arduino/PlatformIO toolchain. Sketches are linked at 0x4000, after the
bootloader, so the board sets the reset VTOR there.

The clock generator reports every oscillator as stable and FCACHE reads
as zero (the FSP waits for FCACHEIV to self-clear). serial0 is SCI9,
where Serial goes when the core is built with -DNO_USB; since it stands
in for USB CDC it transmits much faster than 115200 baud. serial1 is SCI2
(Serial1, pins D0/D1).
---
